WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:05.490
So it's a new week and we are essentially
at the start of the 2020 election right now.

00:00:05.490 --> 00:00:09.320
Now, of course, we've been figuring out who's
going to be the Democratic nominee.

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:12.330
People have been campaigning for a year now.

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:17.210
But what I mean is we are now just weeks,
as I told you last week, from the first votes,

00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:22.569
early voting and absentee voting starting
in at least three states in just over five

00:00:22.569 --> 00:00:23.569
weeks.

00:00:23.569 --> 00:00:27.999
So we need to have a very precise plan for
the next five weeks.

00:00:27.999 --> 00:00:31.480
And, of course, for the three months until
the November election.

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:36.930
And the plan as much as being an offensive
plan against Donald Trump in order to remove

00:00:36.930 --> 00:00:40.390
Donald Trump, the left needs a defensive plan
as well.

00:00:40.390 --> 00:00:46.010
And I mean defense against self-destructive
elements of the left so that we don't self-destruct

00:00:46.010 --> 00:00:50.750
and allow Donald Trump to get another four
years in office, which would be I mean, listen,

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:51.750
I don't want to be hyperbolic.

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:55.790
I don't even want to assign language to it
right now because it's not the point of this

00:00:55.790 --> 00:00:56.790
story.

00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:59.040
But another four years of Trump would be very,
very bad.

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:00.260
Let's put it that way.

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:06.409
And one of the things that we have to be very
careful of right now is for the left to avoid

00:01:06.409 --> 00:01:14.590
engaging in fights that right now are irrelevant
and could potentially simply allow Trump to

00:01:14.590 --> 00:01:15.960
get another four years.

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:18.020
My advice for the left.

00:01:18.020 --> 00:01:22.119
First of all, my advice is for the left and
not for the right, because I'm on the left.

00:01:22.119 --> 00:01:24.549
The right is making all sorts of mistakes.

00:01:24.549 --> 00:01:27.719
I hope they continue to make mistakes and
we should let them make mistakes.

00:01:27.719 --> 00:01:29.280
This is not about giving the right advice.

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:32.130
This is about giving the left advice.

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:39.969
But at the same time, we should understand
how certain fights that are right now irrelevant

00:01:39.969 --> 00:01:43.079
don't need to be put aside forever.

00:01:43.079 --> 00:01:46.539
We just need to be thinking carefully about
what we're doing.

00:01:46.539 --> 00:01:48.560
And that's where I want to go first.

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:51.770
This is not a disclaimer, but it is a clarification.

00:01:51.770 --> 00:01:55.350
This is not about compromising progressive
policy or values.

00:01:55.350 --> 00:01:58.920
This is just realizing we have three months
left.

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:00.369
We have to come together.

00:02:00.369 --> 00:02:04.259
These three months are the last thing we have
to remove Donald Trump.

00:02:04.259 --> 00:02:11.930
And we have to put policy differences within
the left that are currently irrelevant aside,

00:02:11.930 --> 00:02:16.190
because if Trump wins our chances of getting
anything done or zero.

00:02:16.190 --> 00:02:22.110
In other words, the intra left debates, if
Trump wins, will be irrelevant for four more

00:02:22.110 --> 00:02:25.790
years, because either way, we're not getting
anything done with Donald Trump in the White

00:02:25.790 --> 00:02:26.790
House.

00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:32.910
Again, if Joe Biden wins, then we go right
back to these disagreements within the left,

00:02:32.910 --> 00:02:36.840
because the point is, what do we want to push
Joe Biden to do?

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:40.150
What can we push Joe Biden to do from the
left?

00:02:40.150 --> 00:02:43.930
And if Democrats were able to take the Senate
in November, which is looking more likely

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:48.430
now than it was a month ago, I'll talk about
that later, it becomes an even more important

00:02:48.430 --> 00:02:49.430
discussion.

00:02:49.430 --> 00:02:55.180
Now, what I'm specifically looking to here
are some of the different wings of the left

00:02:55.180 --> 00:02:57.280
where there are disagreements.

00:02:57.280 --> 00:03:03.590
And what I want is for everybody to understand
that we don't lose anything by postponing

00:03:03.590 --> 00:03:05.930
these disagreements for three months.

00:03:05.930 --> 00:03:09.710
And we do ourselves a lot of good without
harming the movement now.

00:03:09.710 --> 00:03:11.820
I'll give you some examples to make this really
clear.

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:17.280
I don't want this to just remain some vague
thing, socialism versus social democracy.

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:26.100
OK, this has become a very important, popular,
relevant, heated debate on the left lately.

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:28.820
Right now, that debate does nothing for us.

00:03:28.820 --> 00:03:31.180
It actually does nothing for us in two different
ways.

00:03:31.180 --> 00:03:37.541
Number one, whether you want socialism or
social democracy, the next step is social

00:03:37.541 --> 00:03:39.420
democracy from where we are today.

00:03:39.420 --> 00:03:43.560
There's no way the United States is going
to be a socialist country anytime soon.

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:46.760
When Trump warns the Marxists are taking over.

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:48.420
That's not true.

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:52.710
When the right warns the U.S. could become
socialist if Biden wins.

00:03:52.710 --> 00:03:53.710
That's not true.

00:03:53.710 --> 00:03:58.320
And when the socialist left says we could
have a socialist revolution and be a socialist

00:03:58.320 --> 00:04:01.320
country, none of those things are happening
anytime soon.

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:06.830
And so the point is, if you are a socialist,
which I happen not to be, you are going to

00:04:06.830 --> 00:04:10.010
have to come through social democracy to get
to socialism.

00:04:10.010 --> 00:04:12.250
That's the reality with Biden.

00:04:12.250 --> 00:04:16.640
We have the opportunity to get some policy
done that is socially democratic.

00:04:16.640 --> 00:04:21.901
If you look at Biden's ideas on health care,
taxation, climate change, clean energy, they're

00:04:21.901 --> 00:04:23.690
not exactly what I want.

00:04:23.690 --> 00:04:25.510
And I'll address that later.

00:04:25.510 --> 00:04:30.760
But they're closer to the direction that both
Social Democrats and Socialists want to go

00:04:30.760 --> 00:04:32.910
from where we are today.

00:04:32.910 --> 00:04:35.660
So we're not going to finish that fight in
the next three months.

00:04:35.660 --> 00:04:37.090
We're just not.

00:04:37.090 --> 00:04:42.139
Let's get Trump out and then let's start pushing
Biden in the direction we all agree he needs

00:04:42.139 --> 00:04:46.590
to go at some point in the future if we succeed.

00:04:46.590 --> 00:04:49.520
Socialism versus social democracy will be
relevant to policy.

00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:50.990
It's not the next step.

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:52.470
It's not happening in the next three months.

00:04:52.470 --> 00:04:57.850
So why are we going to argue about that right
now when we're trying to remove Donald Trump?

00:04:57.850 --> 00:04:59.440
Just some other little example.

00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:02.650
Here's one that I thought of just looking
at my Twitter this morning.

00:05:02.650 --> 00:05:06.260
There's this journalist, Mehdi Hassan, and
we follow each other on Twitter.

00:05:06.260 --> 00:05:09.680
I've read it, retweeted some of his work that
I think is great.

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:11.270
He's retweeted some of our stuff.

00:05:11.270 --> 00:05:13.720
We're in agreement about many, many things.

00:05:13.720 --> 00:05:15.030
We happen to disagree.

00:05:15.030 --> 00:05:21.220
Meti and I about BTX with respect to Israel,
boycott, divestment, sanctions, movement.

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:23.270
I believe that the movement is counterproductive.

00:05:23.270 --> 00:05:26.880
I don't think it'll lead to the kind of change
I want to see.

00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:28.980
Mehdi Hassan supports Beedi.

00:05:28.980 --> 00:05:29.980
Yes.

00:05:29.980 --> 00:05:30.980
Great.

00:05:30.980 --> 00:05:31.980
It's a disagreement.

00:05:31.980 --> 00:05:35.350
It's a completely irrelevant one for the next
three months because we have a president.

00:05:35.350 --> 00:05:37.980
I think both Meti and I would agree.

00:05:37.980 --> 00:05:42.160
We have a president right now who's in bed
with the worst of the Israeli right and his

00:05:42.160 --> 00:05:47.640
support of Benjamin Netanyahu and has the
worst instincts, period, when it comes to

00:05:47.640 --> 00:05:49.450
the Israeli-Palestinian conflict.

00:05:49.450 --> 00:05:51.980
So we're both against Benjamin Netanyahu.

00:05:51.980 --> 00:05:53.760
We're both against Donald Trump.

00:05:53.760 --> 00:05:54.760
Trump must be removed.

00:05:54.760 --> 00:05:57.120
So why would we argue about.

00:05:57.120 --> 00:06:01.970
Yes for the next three months rather than
focusing on removing Donald Trump?

00:06:01.970 --> 00:06:05.570
Another example which is maybe more relevant
to you in the immediate single payer health

00:06:05.570 --> 00:06:06.570
care.

00:06:06.570 --> 00:06:07.920
Trump is not for single payer.

00:06:07.920 --> 00:06:09.500
Neither is Joe Biden.

00:06:09.500 --> 00:06:14.700
What Joe Biden is proposing is better than
what Donald Trump is proposing.

00:06:14.700 --> 00:06:19.320
And most Democrats in the Senate don't even
support single payer health care right now.

00:06:19.320 --> 00:06:24.900
So for the next three months, why would we
make the dividing line?

00:06:24.900 --> 00:06:27.280
Does Biden support single payer or not?

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:28.540
It makes no sense.

00:06:28.540 --> 00:06:32.820
Either Biden or Trump are going to be inaugurated
on January 20th.

00:06:32.820 --> 00:06:36.450
Health care will improve if Biden gets his
way.

00:06:36.450 --> 00:06:39.350
We can push him to improve it even more, hopefully.

00:06:39.350 --> 00:06:41.040
And with Trump, we get nothing.

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:43.410
We get fewer people covered if Trump gets
his way.

00:06:43.410 --> 00:06:47.510
So what are we doing now for people who are
going to react very negatively to what I'm

00:06:47.510 --> 00:06:48.590
